1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Welcome. Every enterprise AI demo asks the same question:

2
00:00:05,100 --> 00:00:08,500
"How much can the agent do on its own?"

3
00:00:08,600 --> 00:00:13,200
But in healthcare administration — where prior authorization backlogs cost over $30B annually —

4
00:00:13,300 --> 00:00:16,500
that is the wrong question for compliance teams.

5
00:00:16,600 --> 00:00:21,000
A health plan cannot survive an agent leaking PHI or emailing an unapproved care plan.

6
00:00:21,100 --> 00:00:24,500
So we inverted the pitch: This project is not interesting because agents are autonomous.

7
00:00:24,600 --> 00:00:29,500
It is interesting because of what they are structurally unable to do — enforced in code.

8
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:34,500
Here in our Clinical Command Ledger, we inspect our Fleet Agent Registry.

9
00:00:34,600 --> 00:00:39,000
Every agent advertises its scope and explicit autonomy grade.

10
00:00:39,100 --> 00:00:43,500
Both the Payer Intelligence and Clinical Growth agents are registered as "drafts_only".

11
00:00:43,600 --> 00:00:48,000
Zero tools in their catalog contain "send" or "dispatch" in their names.

12
00:00:48,100 --> 00:00:52,500
Crucially, roles are server-derived from the X-Fleet-Token header.

13
00:00:52,600 --> 00:00:57,000
No tool function accepts a role or employee_id parameter.

14
00:00:57,100 --> 00:01:02,000
The Gemini model literally lacks the vocabulary to claim or escalate permissions.

15
00:01:02,100 --> 00:01:06,500
This guarantee is enforced by automated reflection unit tests across every tool.

16
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:12,000
Now let me trace a query through our asynchronous event stream.

17
00:01:12,100 --> 00:01:16,500
When a claim event or policy query arrives, the Fleet Coordinator routes it through a two-stage pipeline.

18
00:01:16,600 --> 00:01:21,000
Stage 1 is security: A SQL WHERE predicate executes first, filtering unauthorized documents.

19
00:01:21,100 --> 00:01:26,000
If a Clinician requests confidential Payer fee schedules, they receive an empty result set.

20
00:01:26,100 --> 00:01:30,500
Stage 2 is quality: Vector cosine similarity ranks the permitted candidates.

21
00:01:30,600 --> 00:01:35,500
Gemini 3.5 Flash through Vertex AI synthesizes a grounded answer.

22
00:01:35,600 --> 00:01:40,500
Every response MUST cite its source document ID, such as PAY-POL-101.

23
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:46,000
Next, let's look at how we protect external communications using our Isolated Human Approval Gate.

24
00:01:46,100 --> 00:01:51,000
The Payer Agent drafts a Prior Authorization packet complete with an HL7 FHIR v4 Claim Bundle.

25
00:01:51,100 --> 00:01:55,500
But drafting is the end of its reach. Sending and dispatching are HTTP-only endpoints.

26
00:01:55,600 --> 00:02:00,500
Watch what happens when an unapproved premature dispatch is attempted:

27
00:02:00,600 --> 00:02:05,500
The system refuses with an HTTP 409 Conflict error.

28
00:02:05,600 --> 00:02:10,000
No unapproved draft can ever reach a patient or payer.

29
00:02:10,500 --> 00:02:15,500
Now, our Chief Medical Officer logs in via server identity.

30
00:02:15,600 --> 00:02:20,500
As a human supervisor, Dr. Pendelton inspects the HL7 FHIR bundle.

31
00:02:20,600 --> 00:02:25,000
He clicks "Approve" followed by "Dispatch", executing via HTTP status 200.

32
00:02:25,100 --> 00:02:30,000
In addition, our Bulk Dry-Run Simulation Engine allows teams to stress-test batch claim events.

33
00:02:30,100 --> 00:02:35,000
100% of these interactions — including refusals — are logged to an append-only Audit Trail.

34
00:02:35,500 --> 00:02:40,000
Finally, our /metrics endpoint exposes real-time Prometheus Stream Health.

35
00:02:40,100 --> 00:02:45,000
Tracking stream compliance ratios and active agent counts for OpenTelemetry monitoring.

36
00:02:45,100 --> 00:02:50,000
By combining Gemini 3.5 Flash, Google ADK, SQL pre-filtering, and HTTP 409 gates,

37
00:02:50,100 --> 00:02:55,000
we built a zero-trust multi-agent system that proves security in code.

38
00:02:55,100 --> 00:03:00,000
Try the live app at payer-clinical-intelligence.streamlit.app. Thank you!
